cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on Polaris, please cite it as below."
title: "Polaris: a reference implementation of a post-quantum, issuer-unlinkable, compulsion-resistant identity-token system"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khaklin
    given-names: Egor
version: "9.452"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EgorKhaklin/polaris-id"
url: "https://egorkhaklin.github.io/polaris-id/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - digital identity
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - ML-DSA
  - anti-coercion
abstract: >-
  A working reference implementation of an identity-token system whose
  guarantees are enforced in the database schema: post-quantum signatures
  (ML-DSA-65 by default, ML-DSA-87 accepted), zero-knowledge verification with
  an independent second witness, an append-only audit of record, duress-resistant
  operation, and an institutional protocol of signed statements (a registry, a
  trust list, exchange receipts, timestamps, signed documents, a credential-bound
  login token, offline wallet presentations) verified offline by a detached
  verifier and two SDKs against a frozen, conformance-tested wire specification.
  The cryptographic claim is algorithm AGILITY under an audited migration path --
  the algorithm is a row in the schema, not a constant, and migration runs on
  every push -- and not settled security against a quantum adversary; the default
  signing path writes a labelled placeholder unless real ML-DSA is enabled. Both
  limits, and what a break in Module-LWE would and would not cost, are stated in
  docs/PRODUCTION-READINESS.md.
  Educational; notional data only; never deployed.
